# .github/CODEOWNERS
#
# Anyone who can merge a change under .github/ can rewrite the entire CI
# security posture: relax a gate, add a publishing step, widen a token. That
# makes this directory a higher-trust boundary than the source it builds.
#
# Combined with the develop-and-main-protection ruleset, which already requires
# a pull request and a passing quality gate, this ensures a change to the
# pipeline's own controls is reviewed rather than merged by whoever touched it.
#
# The policies are the same class of artifact: they decide what the codebase is
# allowed to be, so a change to them must not ride along unnoticed in a feature
# PR.
